     '29–60 d: UA, blood culture, IM; LP if IM abnormal; PECARN / Step-by-Step rules in Scores',
     'HSV risk (vesicles, seizures, hypothermia, ↑ ALT, maternal HSV) → HSV PCR (blood, CSF, surface swabs); a positive viral test (RSV, influenza, COVID) does not exclude UTI',
