 tx:['Plan A (no dehydration): extra fluids – ORS after each loose stool (< 2 y 50–100 mL; 2–10 y 100–200 mL), zinc, continue feeding [V]',
     'Plan B (some dehydration): ORS 75 mL/kg over 4 h in the ED, reassess (volumes in Scores) [V]',
     'Plan C (severe): IV PLR (or PNSS) 100 mL/kg – < 12 mo 30 mL/kg in 1 h then 70 mL/kg in 5 h; ≥ 12 mo 30 mL/kg in 30 min then 70 mL/kg in 2½ h; ORS by NGT 20 mL/kg/h × 6 h if no IV [V]',
     'Zinc 10 mg/day (< 6 mo) or 20 mg/day (≥ 6 mo) × 10–14 days [V]; ondansetron 0.15 mg/kg once for vomiting (≥ 6 mo) [V]',
     'No antidiarrheals (loperamide) in children; antibiotics only for dysentery (ciprofloxacin or azithromycin) or suspected cholera with severe dehydration [V]; severe acute malnutrition → separate protocol (ReSoMal, slow IV)'],
 txs:'WHO 2005 · DOH IMCI (PH) · ESPGHAN 2014 (intl)',
